The files under fixtures/ come from these projects, unchanged; the fixtures
named in generate.py that copy them (nexus_named) copy them unchanged. Their
sources, with checksums, are in fixtures.toml.

fixtures/nexus_examples/example.h5 and
fixtures/nexus_examples/simple_example_basic.nexus.hdf5 are example files of
the NeXus manual, from https://github.com/nexusformat/definitions
(manual/source/examples/). Copyright the NeXus International Advisory
Committee and contributors. The repository's README states its licence as
the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 3 (accepted by @weber,
2026-11-12); the text is in
licences/LGPL.nexusformat, copied from the repository's LGPL.txt, and the GNU
General Public License it builds on in licences/COPYING.rosettasciio.

fixtures/hyperspy/example2_v3.1.hspy and fixtures/hyperspy/with_lists_etc.hdf5
are test files of RosettaSciIO (https://github.com/hyperspy/rosettasciio),
from its tag v0.15.0, rsciio/tests/data/hspy/. Copyright 2007-2026 The
HyperSpy developers. They are distributed under the GNU General Public
License, version 3 or (at your option) any later version, as RosettaSciIO is;
the text is in licences/COPYING.rosettasciio, copied from RosettaSciIO's
COPYING.txt.

fixtures/h5py_dtypes/ holds test files of h5py (https://github.com/h5py/h5py,
h5py/tests/data_files/), under h5py's BSD 3-Clause licence, in
licences/LICENSE.h5py.

fixtures/matlab/ holds test files of SciPy (https://github.com/scipy/scipy,
scipy/io/matlab/tests/data/), under SciPy's BSD 3-Clause licence, in
licences/LICENSE.scipy.

fixtures/notebooks/ holds test files of nbformat
(https://github.com/jupyter/nbformat, tests/), under nbformat's BSD 3-Clause
licence, in licences/LICENSE.nbformat.

fixtures/scripts/ and the files written by generate.py are distributed under
the MIT licence of modama-formats-common; see ../../../../LICENSE.
